      "content": "Let me read the original test file first.Now let me check the working directory and look for any existing files.Now I have a full picture. I'll write the improved test with these changes:\n- Remove unused constants (`ONE_LONG`, `TWO_LONG`, `THREE_LONG`, `TWO`)\n- Rename `f` to `frequency` for clarity\n- Add structured phase comments explaining what each block does\n- Improve assertion messages to be more specific\n- Replace the cryptic `while` loop with a cleaner for-each styleThe improved test compiled successfully. The refactored version removes the four unused constants, renames `f` to `frequency`, adds phase comments that explain the setup/verify/modify/type-check structure, and gives each assertion a more descriptive message — all without changing any method calls or expected values."
